# /*****************************************************************************/
# * File: synth.ys
# * Author: Olavo Alves Barros Silva
# * Contact: olavo.barros@ufv.com
# * Date: 2026-07-23
# * Description: Yosys script for gaf_encoder - coarse area/cell-count check,
# * not a full technology-mapped synthesis. Run with:
# *   cd src/hw/gaf_encoder && yosys synth.ys
# *
# * Deliberately stops before `techmap`/`abc`: 192 parallel 12x12 multipliers
# * (the outer-product stage) plus the 4096-entry sin_phi ROM make full
# * gate-level logic optimization very slow, and it isn't needed for a
# * quick sanity check anyway - `stat` right after `memory_collect` reports
# * raw cell counts ($mul, $mem, etc.) without expanding them. Real
# * technology-mapped synthesis (LUTs/FFs/DSPs on the actual xc7z020) is
# * Vivado's job later (Task 8 of misc/docs/fpga_implementation_plan.md),
# * not Yosys's here.
# /*****************************************************************************/

read_verilog -sv gaf_encoder.v
hierarchy -check -top gaf_encoder

proc
opt
memory_collect

tee -o area_report.json stat -json
stat

# --- Further steps (commented out - only if a real gate-level estimate is
# needed later; expect this to be slow given the multiplier count above) ---
# synth -flatten
# write_blif -gates gaf_encoder.blif
# abc -liberty <path-to-cell-library>.lib
# stat
